# 3-device fallback — Windows machine unavailable (spec §2.2).
# A second Linux host takes the slave-B role, labeled "降级 3 设备-noWin"
# so downstream analysis knows this run has no cross-OS coverage.

kind: topology
topology_enum: 3-device-nowin
devices:
  - device_kind: laptop
    role: driver
    listen: 127.0.0.1:18092
  - device_kind: headless
    role: observer,slave-a
    listen: 127.0.0.1:18091
  - device_kind: cloud
    role: slave-c
    listen: 127.0.0.1:18093
    vendor: digitalocean
    fallback_label: "降级 3 设备-noWin (Linux 顶替 slave-B; 无 cross-OS 覆盖)"
workloads:
  - cross-device-code-mod
per_workload_reps: 3
notes: |
  Dropped coverage: cross-OS (Windows). windows-only-artifact workload
  becomes stub-only in this config — remove it from the workloads list
  because a Linux slave-B cannot produce Windows-native artifacts.
